---
# aphrody plugin per-project settings — template.
#
# Copy this file to `.claude/aphrody.local.md` at the root of any
# project where you want the plugin's behaviour overridden.
# After editing, restart Claude Code so hooks re-load.
#
# All fields are optional; defaults match production behaviour.

enabled: true                  # set false to disable the plugin in this project
bxc_driver: bun                # bun (default, full /api/* surface) | rust (CDP only)
bxc_port: 8765                 # daemon port (matches BXC_DAEMON_URL default)
bxc_auto_start: true           # auto-spawn `aphrody bxc daemon` on first scrape/tokens call
hooks_blocking: false          # cargo-check hook: false=advisory, true=block on warnings
log_level: info                # debug | info | warn | error
---

# Project notes (free-form)

Anything below the second `---` is treated as free-form context that
the plugin agents can read when relevant. Use it to record :

- which folder of the repo the plugin should focus on
- any project-specific overrides not covered by the frontmatter
- a one-line description of the project for the `/status` summary
